       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum.\n\n- **Daily limit:** The maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg/day in many references) and 2,000\u20132,500 mg/day for extended-release.\n- **Single dose:** 1,700 mg is well above the usual maximum of 850\u20131,000 mg per dose.\n- **Risk:** An overdose raises the risk of lactic acidosis, and that risk doesn't depend on the patient's normal kidney and liver function.\n\nPossible intended orders include:\n- 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- 1,700 mg/day split into two doses (850 mg PO twice daily with meals)\n- 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals\n\nPlease confirm the dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If 1,700 mg three times daily really is what you intend, I can't enter it as written. It would need review by pharmacy or the prescriber of record."
      }
